# Architecture

Read `docs/system/architecture.md` before adding a feature or moving a type across layers. Do not add a dependency that `docs/system/stack.md` does not list.

- One feature is the Gradle module `:feature:<name>`. It contains `domain` and `data` only.
- `domain` depends on the Kotlin standard library. `data` implements domain interfaces and is `internal`. The module exposes a public factory.
- Compose screens live in `:sharedUI` under `com.prodan.taktfinances.<name>`. SwiftUI screens live in `iosApp/iosApp/<Name>/`. Neither imports `data`.
- `:sharedLogic` calls feature factories and exports domain types in the `SharedLogic` iOS framework. App modules only host the process and pass platform ports in.
- A feature does not depend on another feature. A shared type goes in `:core` only when two features must change it together.
- Add a use case only when the action has a rule or coordinates more than one repository call.
- Share a function only when both call sites are the same rule. Leave similar code in place when the reasons to change differ.
- Platform APIs stay in `androidMain`, `iosMain`, or `jvmMain` behind a `commonMain` interface.

```kotlin
interface AccountRepository {
    suspend fun balance(id: AccountId): Money
}

internal class AccountRepositoryImpl(
    private val local: AccountStore,
) : AccountRepository {
    override suspend fun balance(id: AccountId): Money = local.balance(id)
}
```
